        "original_id": "6cd01c79-b7f2-500f-b941-eca5ce459292",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Great Santini, Split Image\n- People: Lewis John Carlino, Pat Conroy, Michael O'Keefe, Ted Kotcheff, Karen Allen, Peter Fonda, James Woods, Elizabeth Ashley, Brian Dennehy, Ronnie Scribner\n- Concepts: tragic hero\n- Roles: Ben Meechum, Danny Noonan\n- Awards: Golden Globe Award for New Star of the Year, Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor\n\nFacts:\n- A tragic hero is the protagonist of a tragedy in drama.\n- Pat Conroy published the novel The Great Santini in 1976.\n- The Great Santini is a 1979 American drama film written and directed by Lewis John Carlino and based on Pat Conroy's 1976 novel of the same name.\n- Michael O'Keefe was born Raymond Peter O'Keefe, Jr. on April 24, 1955, and he is an American film and television actor.\n- Michael O'Keefe is known for playing Danny Noonan in Caddyshack and Ben Meechum in The Great Santini.\n- Michael O'Keefe received a Golden Globe Award for New Star of the Year and an Academy Award nomination for Best Supporting Actor for his role in The Great Santini.\n- Ted Kotcheff directed the film Split Image.\n- Split Image stars Michael O'Keefe, Karen Allen, Peter Fonda, James Woods, Elizabeth Ashley, Brian Dennehy, and Ronnie Scribner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
